Flow facilities, boundaries, blockage and inlet quality (@fd-facility: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../sources/Experimental-Methods-in-Fluids-Mondal.lingua#r_4XFYEGQVB1EV4QF9BP17ME04Y4", #source "../sources/Gas-Dynamics-Kulkarni.lingua#r_34YGDV61X77JFYZH8X8NGDBS9W", #source "../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Mechanics-MIT-2-25.lingua#r_1ZVEYBFSRC755ASSQ2X87MD8VZ", #fluid-dynamics "An-experiment-that-can-distinguish-two-fluid-explanations.lingua#r_15XFDRGDYQY3VKWT8X5V9SXNN9") { r_36W31R46PFWQP6483RTVS3404Z
**Read:** [Experimental Methods in Fluid Mechanics — Pranab K. Mondal](../sources/Experimental-Methods-in-Fluids-Mondal.lingua#r_4XFYEGQVB1EV4QF9BP17ME04Y4), experimental-system and flow-angle treatments; [Gas Dynamics — Vinayak Kulkarni](../sources/Gas-Dynamics-Kulkarni.lingua#r_34YGDV61X77JFYZH8X8NGDBS9W), high-speed testing facilities; [Advanced Fluid Mechanics — MIT 2.25, Fall 2013](../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Mechanics-MIT-2-25.lingua#r_1ZVEYBFSRC755ASSQ2X87MD8VZ), similarity and experimental interpretation problems.

A wind tunnel, water channel, pipe loop or rotating tank creates boundary conditions through real equipment. Inlet profile, turbulence, temperature, pressure, wall motion and downstream control belong to the experiment, even if the analytical model treats them as simple constants or an infinite domain.

Draw the complete facility from reservoir or ambient intake through the test section and return/outlet. Account for contraction, screens, flow conditioning, temperature changes and measuring devices where present. Estimate blockage and wall influence on a nominally unbounded body, and establish the actual development length before assuming a fully developed flow.

Characterize the empty facility before measuring a specimen. Repeat with a changed operating point or model scale to distinguish facility effects from the intended physical response. A simulation fitted to the nominal inlet can disagree with an experiment because the realized inlet is different; preserve measured boundary evidence rather than adjusting the closure until one force matches.

**Continue:** [An experiment that can distinguish two fluid explanations](An-experiment-that-can-distinguish-two-fluid-explanations.lingua#r_15XFDRGDYQY3VKWT8X5V9SXNN9).

